      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, you need to immediately activate the emergency cooling protocols, which are the only way to stop the temperature from rising, but you must do this while keeping your eyes on the gauges to ensure the system isn't overheating from the stress of the failure. While you're doing that, you should call the logistics coordinator to inform them of the situation, but make sure to tell them the exact location of the truck so the nearest garrison can be alerted to the potential spoilage.\n\nRegarding the tuna, you need to check the internal temperature of the cargo immediately, but be careful not to open the doors too many times, as every time you open the door, the cold air escapes and the heat rushes in like a swarm of hungry goblins. If the temperature has already climbed above the safe threshold, you must initiate the emergency freezing protocol, which involves dumping the water into the freezer tanks to create a rapid chill, but you must ensure the water doesn't freeze the sensors, which could be a disaster if the sensors are too sensitive.\n\nYou also need to check the food safety protocols, specifically the HACCP plan, but you should review it with a colleague who knows the goblin laws on food preservation, because if the temperature stays above",
